2
00:09:33,913 --> 00:09:39,913
Stepfather 3 is a horror, thriller, tv movie film directed by Guy Magar.

3
00:14:20,869 --> 00:14:26,869
After escaping a Puget Sound institution, "Stepfather" Gene Clifford alters his
appearance with plastic surgery and takes on another new identity: Keith Grant.

4
00:19:07,826 --> 00:19:13,826
Moving to Deer View, California, Keith falls for a divorced school principal,
arousing the suspicions of her wheelchair-bound, computer-savvy son.

5
00:23:54,782 --> 00:24:00,782
Keith Grant / The Stepfather, played by Robert Wightman.

6
00:28:41,739 --> 00:28:47,739
Christine Ann Davis, played by Priscilla Barnes.

7
00:33:28,695 --> 00:33:34,695
Jennifer Ashley, played by Season Hubley.

8
00:38:15,652 --> 00:38:21,652
Andy Davis, played by David Tom.

9
00:43:02,608 --> 00:43:08,608
Father Ernest Thomas Brennan, played by John Ingle.

10
00:47:49,565 --> 00:47:55,565
Mr. Thompson, played by Dennis Paladino.

11
00:52:36,521 --> 00:52:42,521
The Stepfather is a 1987 American psychological horror film directed by Joseph
Ruben and starring Terry O'Quinn, Jill Schoelen, and Shelley Hack.

12
00:57:23,478 --> 00:57:29,478
O'Quinn stars as an identity-assuming serial killer who
marries a widow with a teenage daughter.

13
01:02:10,434 --> 01:02:16,434
Having killed his previous family and changed his identity, his murderous
tendencies continue after his stepdaughter becomes suspicious of him.

14
01:06:57,391 --> 01:07:03,391
The film is loosely based on the life of mass murderer John List, although the
plot is more commonly associated with slasher films of the era.

15
01:11:44,347 --> 01:11:50,347
The film was written by Donald E.

16
01:16:31,304 --> 01:16:37,304
Westlake, from a story by Westlake, Carolyn Lefcourt and Brian Garfield (the latter
of Death Wish fame), with an uncredited rewrite by David Loughery.

17
01:21:18,260 --> 01:21:24,260
The film was theatrically released in the United States on January 23, 1987.

18
01:26:05,217 --> 01:26:11,217
It grossed $2.5 million at the box office and was well-received by critics.

19
01:30:52,173 --> 01:30:58,173
It has since gained a cult following and was followed by two slasher
sequels, Stepfather II (1989) and Stepfather III (1992).

20
01:35:39,130 --> 01:35:45,130
A remake, also called The Stepfather, was released in 2009.

21
01:40:26,086 --> 01:40:32,086
The film explores themes of stepfather, sequel, serial killer.

22
01:45:13,043 --> 01:45:19,043
The tone is dark and emotional and intense.
